# XSH sigaddset()
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.

assertion  XSH.sigaddset.001
anchor     functions/sigaddset.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      1988
says       On an empty set, sigaddset() of SIGUSR1, then of SIGTERM, returns 0
           each time; afterwards those two are members and no other table
           signal is.
uses       XSH.sigismember.001
test       t/001-adds-one.c

assertion  XSH.sigaddset.002
anchor     functions/sigaddset.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2008
says       On an empty set, sigaddset() of SIGRTMIN and of SIGRTMAX returns 0
           and makes each a member, and SIGRTMIN+1 stays out (when it is
           below SIGRTMAX).
uses       XSH.sigismember.001
test       t/002-adds-rt.c
